<!-- Holafly vs SimLocal Comparison Content -->
<div class="content-section">

  {% set holaflyPrimary = providerA.codes | findCode(providerA.primaryCode) %}
  {% set simlocalPrimary = providerB.codes | findCode(providerB.primaryCode) %}

  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Pick <strong>Holafly</strong> if you want one flat unlimited-data price and never want to think about a gigabyte cap, anywhere across its 200+ destinations. Pick <strong>SimLocal</strong> if you're headed to the UK specifically and want a real UK phone number bundled into your plan, plus a no-questions-asked refund if it doesn't work out. They're not really chasing the same traveler.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: Unlimited Everywhere vs. a Bundled UK Number</h2>
  <p>
    Holafly's whole pitch is unlimited data at a flat price per day, per country or region, with no gigabyte counting. SimLocal sells fixed-GB plans instead, but its UK plans come with something Holafly doesn't offer at all: a real UK phone number for calls and texts, not just a data-only eSIM. If a UK trip is the plan and you want to actually receive calls and texts on a UK number, SimLocal does something Holafly structurally can't. If the trip spans multiple countries and you'd rather not track usage, Holafly's flat unlimited price is the simpler option.
  </p>
  <p>
    Neither provider is a one-size-fits-all pick. SimLocal also sells student-specific plans for longer stays and runs a small footprint of airport kiosks (confirmed at Heathrow), which Holafly doesn't have an equivalent to. Holafly's standout is a built-in VPN on its China eSIM, which SimLocal's plans don't offer.
  </p>

  <h2>Feature Snapshot</h2>
  <div class="content-box">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Feature</th>
          <th>Holafly</th>
          <th>SimLocal</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Pricing model</td><td>Unlimited data, flat price per day/region</td><td>Fixed-GB plans by country or region</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Destinations</td><td>200+</td><td>200+</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Local phone number</td><td>Not offered</td><td>Most UK plans include a free UK number</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Refund policy</td><td>No blanket guarantee advertised</td><td>"No Quibble Refunds," no explanation required</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Live support channel</td><td>Website live chat, 24/7</td><td>WhatsApp, email, help centre, 24/7 (no site chat widget)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>China eSIM</td><td>Built-in VPN</td><td>No equivalent offering</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="content-note">SimLocal doesn't publish per-country GB pricing the way some competitors do, so this is a feature comparison rather than a side-by-side price table.</p>
  </div>

