    <ul>
      <li><strong>Holafly:</strong> {{ providerA.primaryCode }}, {{ holaflyPrimary.discount | lower }}. <a href="/holafly/">Full code list &rarr;</a></li>
      <li><strong>SimLocal:</strong> {{ providerB.primaryCode }}, {{ simlocalPrimary.discount | lower }}. <a href="/simlocal/">Full code list &rarr;</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:.75rem;margin-bottom:0;color:#63553F;">Both codes are ours, so we show them first on their own pages. SimLocal's ADAMANDLINDS beats its four other public codes, which only give 5%.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Is Holafly or SimLocal the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with Holafly if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You're traveling to multiple countries and don't want to track data per stop</li>
        <li>You genuinely don't know how much data you'll use</li>
        <li>China is on the itinerary and you want the built-in VPN</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with SimLocal if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You're headed to the UK and want a real UK number for calls and texts</li>
        <li>You want a no-questions refund if the eSIM doesn't work out</li>
        <li>You're studying abroad and want a plan built for a longer stay</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>SimLocal's phone number only comes with its UK plans.</strong> It isn't a universal feature across every SimLocal destination, so check the specific plan page if a real local number matters to you outside the UK. Holafly doesn't offer a bundled number on any plan, in the UK or elsewhere; it's a data-only eSIM across the board.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Holafly's "unlimited" and SimLocal's fixed-GB plans both apply fair-use limits eventually,</strong> just at different points. Holafly can slow speeds after very heavy same-day use on some plans; SimLocal's plans simply run out of the GB you bought, same as most fixed-data sellers. Neither is a trap, but "unlimited" doesn't mean "unmanaged" on Holafly's side.
  </p>
  <p>
    Want a cheaper fixed-GB alternative to SimLocal with a different kind of bundled number instead? See our <a href="/compare/simlocal-vs-bytesim/">SimLocal vs ByteSIM comparison</a>. For device setup and eSIM basics that apply to both providers, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Holafly vs SimLocal FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, Holafly or SimLocal</h3>
      <p>It depends on usage and destination. SimLocal's GB-capped plans can work out cheaper for light, single-country use, especially in the UK where the free bundled phone number adds value. Holafly's flat unlimited price is better value the heavier your data use gets, or across a multi-country trip.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does SimLocal offer a phone number outside the UK</h3>
      <p>Most of SimLocal's UK plans include a real UK number for calls and texts. That's specific to the UK lineup; check the plan page for other destinations before assuming the same feature applies.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I get a refund if I change my mind</h3>
      <p>SimLocal advertises a "No Quibble Refunds" policy, no explanation required. Holafly doesn't advertise an equivalent blanket guarantee.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which one is better for a trip to China</h3>
      <p>Holafly, if you don't want to set up a separate VPN: its China eSIM has one built in. SimLocal has no equivalent, so you'd need your own VPN solution regardless of plan.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

